--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shipped knowledge corpora
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/toolchains/pango-pds/knowledge/ contains data generated by
`pnpm knowledge:build` from a locally installed Pango Design Suite:

  primitives/  primitives.index.json
      Module names, port names/directions/widths and parameter defaults parsed
      from the Logos2 primitive library. Structural interface facts, not the
      vendor's implementation or documentation prose.

  ip/  ip.index.json
      IP core names, versions, supported device lists and parameter names parsed
      from the PDS IP catalog's index.xml files. Same character as above.
      `datasheet` fields are PATHS into your own install, stored relative to the
      install root; no datasheet content is included.

  doc-chunks/  docs.index.json
      doc-chunks/ is chunked text from this repository's OWN skill notes under
      skills/ — authored by the contributors, covered by LICENSE.
      docs.index.json is a registry of PDF paths inside your own PDS install,
      again relative and content-free.

These corpora are regenerable from your own licensed install and carry no
vendor documentation text. Regenerate after changing PDS version or machine.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deliberately NOT shipped
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/toolchains/modelsim/knowledge/commands.index.json is built from
<modelsimHome>/docs/cmd_help/*.txt, which is Siemens EDA product documentation
delivered under the ModelSim/Questa EULA. That text is not redistributed with
this project. `fpga_msim_doc_search` reports the corpus as unbuilt until you
generate it from your own licensed install:

    pnpm knowledge:build:msim

The output is gitignored and stays on your machine.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hardware protocol implementations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/toolchains/pango-pds/jtag/ implements IEEE 1149.1 TAP traversal over FTDI
MPSSE, and the vendor's documented PANGO200 JTAG-FLA access sequence and trigger
encoding. It contains no vendor source code.
